{
    "title": "Hallow: Prayer & Meditation",
    "description": "** The #1 Prayer App & #1 Catholic App**\r\n\r\nWHAT IS HALLOW\r\nHallow is a Christian prayer app that offers audio-guided meditation sessions to help us grow in our Christian faith & spiritual lives and find peace in God. Explore over 10,000 different sessions on contemplative prayer, meditation, Catholic Holy Bible readings, music, and more.\r\n\r\nIn today\u2019s world, we\u2019re stressed, anxious, distracted, and often sleep-deprived. At the same time, we\u2019re searching for deeper meaning, purpose & relationships. We believe these two challenges can be addressed with the same solution: peace in Jesus. In the end, after all, a halo in Heaven is the goal :)\r\n\r\nWHAT YOU GET\r\n\u2022 Daily Prayers & Devotionals: Pray daily across methods, including 3 of our most popular \u2013 Lectio Divina (in Daily Readings), the Holy Rosary, the Divine Mercy Chaplet, or Daily Mass Readings and Reflections.\r\n\u2022 Christian Meditation: Similar to mindfulness meditation in learning to be comfortable in silence. But in Christian meditation, the goal is never to remain in ourselves, always to lift our hearts & minds to God, to talk with Him, listen to Him, and recognize His presence with us\r\n\u2022 Bible Stories for Sleep: Try sounds of the Night Prayer from Liturgy of the Hours/Daily Office and Catholic Holy Bible stories read by folks like Jonathan Roumie from The Chosen or Father Mike Schmitz from The Bible in a Year podcast\r\n\u2022 Rosary: Meditate with Mary through the mysteries of the Catholic Rosary and other daily devotionals and prayers.\r\n\u2022 Ignatian Examen: Reflect & meditate on your day and find an awareness of God, Jesus Christ, and the Holy Spirit\r\n\u2022 Lectio Divina: Converse with God through passages/Scripture from the Holy Bible\r\n\u2022 Taiz\u00e9 & Gregorian Chant: Calm, meditative chants, Christian music & sleep sounds\r\n\u2022 Community: Join the #Pray40 Lent Challenge from Ash Wednesday to Easter, or our #Pray25 Advent Challenge for Christmas\r\n\u2022 Homilies & Guests: From Fr. Mike Schmitz, Bishop Barron, and more on topics like being a Catholic Dad, family & more!\r\n\u2022 Praylists: Sessions on joy, humility, discernment, stress reduction, and calm sleep meditations\r\n\u2022 Personal Prayer Journal: Pray, meditate & document your spiritual journey\r\n\u2022 Challenges: Join thousands of Catholics and Christians in a community of prayer such as Easter Prayers, Divine Mercy Chaplet, or 54-Day Rosary Novena.\r\n\u2022 Litanies, Novenas, & Devotionals: Try the Litany of Humility, the Surrender Novena & more!\r\n\u2022 Minute Meditations: Jesus, I Trust in You; Angelus; Holy Rosary Decade; St. Michael the Archangel prayer & more!\r\n\r\nAdditional features to customize your prayer experience:\r\n\u2022 3 different length options for each prayer (typically 5, 10, or 15 minutes)\r\n\u2022 Set prayer reminders to pray and journal\r\n\u2022 Include calm background music like Gregorian chant\r\n\u2022 Download & listen offline\r\n\u2022 Join a Hallow Family to share prayers, intentions, and journal reflections with one another\r\n\r\nAs Hallow is a Prayer App, the content is developed by experienced Catholic theology & spirituality guides, reviewed by senior leaders within the Catholic Church (e.g., PhDs, professors, Bishops, authors), and based on content from the approved Catholic Bible. While Hallow can be a beautiful app for Catholics, it is meant as a resource for people of all faiths & religions.\r\n\r\nSUBSCRIPTION PRICING AND TERMS\r\nUsers can access our daily audio prayers including the Rosary and Bible in a Year for free.\r\nTo access the full suite of Hallow, we offer two auto-renewing subscription options (US customers prices):\r\n$9.99 per month\r\n$69.99 per year\r\n\r\nYour Hallow subscription will renew automatically unless auto-renew is turned off at least 24 hours before the end of the current period. You can go to your Google Play account settings to manage your subscription and turn off auto-renew. Your account will be charged when the purchase is confirmed.\r\n\r\nTerms and conditions: https://hallow.app/terms-of-service\r\nPrivacy policy: https://hallow.app/privacy-policy",
    "descriptionHTML": "** The #1 Prayer App &amp; #1 Catholic App**<br><br>WHAT IS HALLOW<br>Hallow is a Christian prayer app that offers audio-guided meditation sessions to help us grow in our Christian faith &amp; spiritual lives and find peace in God. Explore over 10,000 different sessions on contemplative prayer, meditation, Catholic Holy Bible readings, music, and more.<br><br>In today\u2019s world, we\u2019re stressed, anxious, distracted, and often sleep-deprived. At the same time, we\u2019re searching for deeper meaning, purpose &amp; relationships. We believe these two challenges can be addressed with the same solution: peace in Jesus. In the end, after all, a halo in Heaven is the goal :)<br><br>WHAT YOU GET<br>\u2022 Daily Prayers &amp; Devotionals: Pray daily across methods, including 3 of our most popular \u2013 Lectio Divina (in Daily Readings), the Holy Rosary, the Divine Mercy Chaplet, or Daily Mass Readings and Reflections.<br>\u2022 Christian Meditation: Similar to mindfulness meditation in learning to be comfortable in silence. But in Christian meditation, the goal is never to remain in ourselves, always to lift our hearts &amp; minds to God, to talk with Him, listen to Him, and recognize His presence with us<br>\u2022 Bible Stories for Sleep: Try sounds of the Night Prayer from Liturgy of the Hours/Daily Office and Catholic Holy Bible stories read by folks like Jonathan Roumie from The Chosen or Father Mike Schmitz from The Bible in a Year podcast<br>\u2022 Rosary: Meditate with Mary through the mysteries of the Catholic Rosary and other daily devotionals and prayers.<br>\u2022 Ignatian Examen: Reflect &amp; meditate on your day and find an awareness of God, Jesus Christ, and the Holy Spirit<br>\u2022 Lectio Divina: Converse with God through passages/Scripture from the Holy Bible<br>\u2022 Taiz\u00e9 &amp; Gregorian Chant: Calm, meditative chants, Christian music &amp; sleep sounds<br>\u2022 Community: Join the #Pray40 Lent Challenge from Ash Wednesday to Easter, or our #Pray25 Advent Challenge for Christmas<br>\u2022 Homilies &amp; Guests: From Fr. Mike Schmitz, Bishop Barron, and more on topics like being a Catholic Dad, family &amp; more!<br>\u2022 Praylists: Sessions on joy, humility, discernment, stress reduction, and calm sleep meditations<br>\u2022 Personal Prayer Journal: Pray, meditate &amp; document your spiritual journey<br>\u2022 Challenges: Join thousands of Catholics and Christians in a community of prayer such as Easter Prayers, Divine Mercy Chaplet, or 54-Day Rosary Novena.<br>\u2022 Litanies, Novenas, &amp; Devotionals: Try the Litany of Humility, the Surrender Novena &amp; more!<br>\u2022 Minute Meditations: Jesus, I Trust in You; Angelus; Holy Rosary Decade; St. Michael the Archangel prayer &amp; more!<br><br>Additional features to customize your prayer experience:<br>\u2022 3 different length options for each prayer (typically 5, 10, or 15 minutes)<br>\u2022 Set prayer reminders to pray and journal<br>\u2022 Include calm background music like Gregorian chant<br>\u2022 Download &amp; listen offline<br>\u2022 Join a Hallow Family to share prayers, intentions, and journal reflections with one another<br><br>As Hallow is a Prayer App, the content is developed by experienced Catholic theology &amp; spirituality guides, reviewed by senior leaders within the Catholic Church (e.g., PhDs, professors, Bishops, authors), and based on content from the approved Catholic Bible. While Hallow can be a beautiful app for Catholics, it is meant as a resource for people of all faiths &amp; religions.<br><br>SUBSCRIPTION PRICING AND TERMS<br>Users can access our daily audio prayers including the Rosary and Bible in a Year for free.<br>To access the full suite of Hallow, we offer two auto-renewing subscription options (US customers prices):<br>$9.99 per month<br>$69.99 per year<br><br>Your Hallow subscription will renew automatically unless auto-renew is turned off at least 24 hours before the end of the current period. You can go to your Google Play account settings to manage your subscription and turn off auto-renew. Your account will be charged when the purchase is confirmed.<br><br>Terms and conditions: https://hallow.app/terms-of-service<br>Privacy policy: https://hallow.app/privacy-policy",
